• Data Extraction (.map(Function))
Transforms elements from one type or structure to another.

• Intermediate Ops (.filter(), .map(), .sorted())
Returns a new stream. These are lazy and do not execute until a terminal operation is called.

• Terminal Ops (.collect(), .count(), .findFirst())
Consumes the stream, triggers the execution pipeline, and yields a final result or side-effect.

• Null Safety (Optional<T>)
A container that explicitly handles optional or missing values without throwing null pointer exceptions.

• Lazy Evaluation (Deferred Execution)
Delays the evaluation of the pipeline until a terminal operation is invoked, enabling efficiency and short-circuiting.

• Sorting (.sorted(Comparator))
Reorders stream elements based on natural ordering or custom comparator logic.

• Collecting (.collect(Collectors.to...))
Accumulates elements into a standard Java collection like a List, Set, or Map.

• Grouping (Collectors.groupingBy())
Groups elements by a key function into a Map<K, List<V>>.

• Partitioning (Collectors.partitioningBy())
Splits elements by a boolean predicate into a Map<Boolean, List<V>>.
